# PIMID (1.12.109): a 1T1R RRAM cell (one CMOS access transistor per cell), the RRAM cell of NVMExplorer
# (Pentecost, Hankin, Donato, Hempstead, Wei, Brooks, HPCA 2022; repository data/cell_cfgs/RRAM.cell and
# cell_cfgs.py RRAMCellConfig defaults): 53 F^2 and a 6 F access transistor, its reference cell being
# derived from TSMC's N40 1T1R macro (Chou et al., ISSCC 2018). The resistances, read and SET/RESET
# values are NVSim's sample_RRAM.cell values, as that repository states. Every published 22-40 nm RRAM
# macro (TSMC N40 and N22, Intel 22FFL) is 1T1R.
-MemCellType: memristor

-CellArea (F^2): 53
-CellAspectRatio: 1

# PIMID (1.12.244): the resistances of a 1T1R storage cell of the referenced 40 nm family, LRS about 10 kOhm and HRS
# about 100 kOhm (Chiang, Ni, Sung, Hou, Chang, Jou, "Hardware-Robust In-RRAM-Computing for Object Detection",
# arXiv 2205.03996, on a TSMC 40 nm RRAM test chip designed for storage: "resistance values of [LRS] and [HRS] from
# storage applications are around 10^4 ohms and 10^5 ohms"), taken at every voltage (the sample's values were a
# selector-less crosspoint cell's, 100 kOhm to 10 MOhm). The half-reset LRS keeps the sample's 5x ratio.
-ResistanceOnAtSetVoltage (ohm): 10000
-ResistanceOffAtSetVoltage (ohm): 100000
-ResistanceOnAtResetVoltage (ohm): 10000
-ResistanceOffAtResetVoltage (ohm): 100000
-ResistanceOnAtReadVoltage (ohm): 10000
-ResistanceOffAtReadVoltage (ohm): 100000
-ResistanceOnAtHalfResetVoltage (ohm): 50000

-CapacitanceOn (F): 1e-16
-CapacitanceOff (F): 1e-16

-ReadMode: current
# PIMID (1.12.244): EMBER reads at 100 mV (Levy et al., JSSC 2024, Fig. 14); read power V^2 / LRS = 1 uW.
-ReadVoltage (V): 0.1
-ReadPower (uW): 1
# PIMID (1.12.244): the read is priced at EMBER's measured macro read energy, 1.0 pJ/bit for 1 b/cell (cell, bitlines,
# sense amplifiers -- half of it -- and decoders; Levy et al., JSSC 2024, Sec. V-A and Fig. 14).
-MacroReadEnergy (pJ/bit): 1.0

-ResetMode: voltage
-ResetVoltage (V): 2.0
-ResetPulse (ns): 10
-ResetEnergy (pJ): 0.6

-SetMode: voltage
-SetVoltage (V): 2.0
-SetPulse (ns): 10
-SetEnergy (pJ): 0.6

-AccessType: CMOS
-AccessCMOSWidth (F): 6

-ReadFloating: false
# PIMID (1.12.162): write-verify (published RRAM macros program with write-verify: Intel 22FFL, Jain et al.
# ISSCC 2019; TSMC, Chou et al. ISSCC 2018 / VLSI 2020). From the one open SLC write-verify
# macro, EMBER (TSMC 40 nm RRAM, Levy et al., JSSC 2024; fits of energy and bandwidth vs pulse count):
# 0.40 nJ/bit at 12.4 Mb/s gives (400 - 41.37) / 27.91 = 12.9 and (80.8 - 0.71) / 6.06 = 13.2 pulse-
# and-verify rounds per word, about 13; and about 9 of 48 cells pulsed per round gives about 3.2 cell
# pulses per bit (Fig. 5.10). Its ISPP starts from 0 V, so these are on the high side.
-WriteVerifyRounds (avg): 13
# PIMID (1.12.244): the time and energy of those rounds, from the same macro's fits against the pulse count R (the
# fits the 13 rounds come from): (0.71 + 6.06 R) ns per bit of a 48-bit word and (41.37 + 27.91 R) pJ per bit,
# 3.82 us and 404 pJ/bit at R = 13 (EMBER measures 12.4 Mb/s and 0.40 nJ/bit). Every 48-bit word of an access has
# its own write-verify engine and the words are written in parallel (EMBER writes one 48-bit word at a
# time per macro; a 512-bit access is taken as 11 such words side by side), so a write takes one word's time. The
# measured energy includes the write supplies, so the pump efficiency below no longer applies to this cell.
-WriteVerifyWordBits: 48
-WriteVerifyFitTime (ns/bit): 0.71 6.06
-WriteVerifyFitEnergy (pJ/bit): 41.37 27.91
-WritePulsesPerBit (avg): 3.2
# PIMID (1.12.163): the write supply. The 2.0 V SET/RESET pulses come from an on-chip charge pump above the
# logic supply (Intel 22FFL, Jain et al. ISSCC 2019: "a single supply coming from an in-situ charge pump").
# Efficiency 0.5: a published on-chip pump measures 52.3 % (conventional) and 63.7 % (charge-sharing dual
# pump) at 0.18 um (Huang, Zhang, Yoshihara, IEICE Trans. Fundamentals E95-A, 2012); a 5 V PCM RESET pump
# is 21.6 % (Jiang et al., ISCA 2014). 0.5 is taken just under the measured pumps.
-WriteSupplyVoltage (V): 2.0
-WritePumpEfficiency (ratio): 0.5
